[{:db/id 17592186179667 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-73c3adf2-10ac-55b7-bd69-23ff8f9e55de" "question-64f65081-673f-5e6a-96c9-e04b5e0fef48"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179668 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3711f78b-b6ea-5fad-94b4-d74bce1c6d90" "question-12857d2d-71a8-5e2b-b97a-e1dbaa816b56" "question-72946120-c877-5902-ac8d-3152b3d1dae6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179727 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a1179d1f-26fd-5e6b-8418-2edcb8c92a44" "question-ffb8ae0d-deff-51a0-b378-8457bd7de602" "question-450ac2a6-bf41-5a0f-9075-7209697c621b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-73c3adf2-10ac-55b7-bd69-23ff8f9e55de" :question/id #uuid "73c3adf2-10ac-55b7-bd69-23ff8f9e55de" :question/math-academy-id "q-75333" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,4]\\times [3,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=4x+7y-16.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=4x+7y-16$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=4x+7y-16$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=4{x}_{i}+7{y}_{j}-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i}+7{y}_{j}-16)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4{x}_{i}+7{y}_{j}-16.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-921742fc-31a9-5944-98d7-e5554b79a204"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-921742fc-31a9-5944-98d7-e5554b79a204" :answer-field/id #uuid "921742fc-31a9-5944-98d7-e5554b79a204" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cccdb938-c49b-599f-9fc7-7b3205992cc7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-82743949-e4c2-5a5f-a06e-8ae531089a72" "answer-074e4e05-d3bb-55bd-8816-5010793ff112" "answer-8ccf6694-a8bf-5ca6-bf48-c61e951fbd38" "answer-38f1076b-0cad-5d95-8f49-c8205cd8a58c" "answer-cccdb938-c49b-599f-9fc7-7b3205992cc7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82743949-e4c2-5a5f-a06e-8ae531089a72" :answer/id #uuid "82743949-e4c2-5a5f-a06e-8ae531089a72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-074e4e05-d3bb-55bd-8816-5010793ff112" :answer/id #uuid "074e4e05-d3bb-55bd-8816-5010793ff112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ccf6694-a8bf-5ca6-bf48-c61e951fbd38" :answer/id #uuid "8ccf6694-a8bf-5ca6-bf48-c61e951fbd38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}_{i-1}+7{y}_{j-1}-16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38f1076b-0cad-5d95-8f49-c8205cd8a58c" :answer/id #uuid "38f1076b-0cad-5d95-8f49-c8205cd8a58c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}_{i}+7{y}_{j-1}-16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cccdb938-c49b-599f-9fc7-7b3205992cc7" :answer/id #uuid "cccdb938-c49b-599f-9fc7-7b3205992cc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}_{i}+7{y}_{j}-16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-64f65081-673f-5e6a-96c9-e04b5e0fef48" :question/id #uuid "64f65081-673f-5e6a-96c9-e04b5e0fef48" :question/math-academy-id "q-170677" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,5]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{3}+3{y}^{2}.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{3}+3{y}^{2}$ increases as $x$ increases on $[0,5],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{3}+3{y}^{2}$ increases as $y$ increases on $[1,2].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})={x}_{i}^{3}+3{y}_{i}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}^{3}+3{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i}^{3}+3{y}_{j}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a7c52083-4fc0-551d-9005-b6b5695ed7c5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a7c52083-4fc0-551d-9005-b6b5695ed7c5" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c52083-4fc0-551d-9005-b6b5695ed7c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-95e00436-05f4-56a8-9927-c19fb98ac387" :answer-field/choices ["answer-39b48429-86f0-5bd1-b63e-9b6d2ae4527a" "answer-73a20fd7-73f1-5b55-9db2-aebfb5b89b94" "answer-b625b468-ff56-5299-92eb-fb3b302c3b1d" "answer-dc2717d4-e925-5d12-b936-9d385f403fa1" "answer-95e00436-05f4-56a8-9927-c19fb98ac387"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39b48429-86f0-5bd1-b63e-9b6d2ae4527a" :answer/id #uuid "39b48429-86f0-5bd1-b63e-9b6d2ae4527a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{i+1}^{3}+3{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73a20fd7-73f1-5b55-9db2-aebfb5b89b94" :answer/id #uuid "73a20fd7-73f1-5b55-9db2-aebfb5b89b94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{3}+3{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b625b468-ff56-5299-92eb-fb3b302c3b1d" :answer/id #uuid "b625b468-ff56-5299-92eb-fb3b302c3b1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{3}+3{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc2717d4-e925-5d12-b936-9d385f403fa1" :answer/id #uuid "dc2717d4-e925-5d12-b936-9d385f403fa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{3}+3{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95e00436-05f4-56a8-9927-c19fb98ac387" :answer/id #uuid "95e00436-05f4-56a8-9927-c19fb98ac387" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{3}+3{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3711f78b-b6ea-5fad-94b4-d74bce1c6d90" :question/id #uuid "3711f78b-b6ea-5fad-94b4-d74bce1c6d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-75341" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,1]\\times [-21,-3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=-23-13x-14y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=-23-13x-14y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=-23-13x-14y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/5b/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=-23-13{x}_{i-1}-14{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-23-13{x}_{i-1}-14{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $-23-13{x}_{i-1}-14{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1e8ec810-d71a-586e-b9ba-d36e14915538"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1e8ec810-d71a-586e-b9ba-d36e14915538" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e8ec810-d71a-586e-b9ba-d36e14915538" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1af10802-01e8-590a-8219-dfa60bf29a3f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ffa5ca00-195a-56da-8646-39d8b3dd5266" "answer-dd64272f-e557-588e-9740-b70624c6a86f" "answer-1af10802-01e8-590a-8219-dfa60bf29a3f" "answer-51aa60b8-8024-553e-9794-91961d7d5b05" "answer-4d08e587-3ba3-56a3-9b90-16f3b2efa8f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffa5ca00-195a-56da-8646-39d8b3dd5266" :answer/id #uuid "ffa5ca00-195a-56da-8646-39d8b3dd5266" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-21{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd64272f-e557-588e-9740-b70624c6a86f" :answer/id #uuid "dd64272f-e557-588e-9740-b70624c6a86f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-21{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1af10802-01e8-590a-8219-dfa60bf29a3f" :answer/id #uuid "1af10802-01e8-590a-8219-dfa60bf29a3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-23-13{x}_{i-1}-14{y}_{j-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51aa60b8-8024-553e-9794-91961d7d5b05" :answer/id #uuid "51aa60b8-8024-553e-9794-91961d7d5b05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-23-13{x}_{i-1}-14{y}_{j}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d08e587-3ba3-56a3-9b90-16f3b2efa8f0" :answer/id #uuid "4d08e587-3ba3-56a3-9b90-16f3b2efa8f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-23-13{x}_{i}-14{y}_{j}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-12857d2d-71a8-5e2b-b97a-e1dbaa816b56" :question/id #uuid "12857d2d-71a8-5e2b-b97a-e1dbaa816b56" :question/math-academy-id "q-170680" :question/problem "Let $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=-5x-4y-1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=-5x-4y-1$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=-5x-4y-1$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/5b/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=-5{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-5{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1}-1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $-5{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1}-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-883776c9-3922-5bc9-91a9-c6f259c5bd46"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-883776c9-3922-5bc9-91a9-c6f259c5bd46" :answer-field/id #uuid "883776c9-3922-5bc9-91a9-c6f259c5bd46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-894e2f98-1d44-52c6-89a0-57a6513ae71a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e7f29303-f8fe-5b0b-be18-d8f15f3cf8e7" "answer-ffae09d1-4816-5db6-b1c9-48739f065af0" "answer-894e2f98-1d44-52c6-89a0-57a6513ae71a" "answer-4326c2d1-f5f9-594f-baa7-909192bb783f" "answer-05c26cb7-e498-58c2-926a-37ddb09c26ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7f29303-f8fe-5b0b-be18-d8f15f3cf8e7" :answer/id #uuid "e7f29303-f8fe-5b0b-be18-d8f15f3cf8e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10{x}_{i-1}-8{y}_{j-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffae09d1-4816-5db6-b1c9-48739f065af0" :answer/id #uuid "ffae09d1-4816-5db6-b1c9-48739f065af0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-894e2f98-1d44-52c6-89a0-57a6513ae71a" :answer/id #uuid "894e2f98-1d44-52c6-89a0-57a6513ae71a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4326c2d1-f5f9-594f-baa7-909192bb783f" :answer/id #uuid "4326c2d1-f5f9-594f-baa7-909192bb783f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5{x}_{i}-4{y}_{j}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05c26cb7-e498-58c2-926a-37ddb09c26ad" :answer/id #uuid "05c26cb7-e498-58c2-926a-37ddb09c26ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{i}-2{y}_{j}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-72946120-c877-5902-ac8d-3152b3d1dae6" :question/id #uuid "72946120-c877-5902-ac8d-3152b3d1dae6" :question/math-academy-id "q-75342" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,1]\\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=15-3{x}^{2}-7{y}^{2}.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=15-3{x}^{2}-7{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=15-3{x}^{2}-7{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[0,1].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/5b/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=15-3{x}_{i-1}^{2}-7{y}_{j-1}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(15-3{x}_{i-1}^{2}-7{y}_{j-1}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $15-3{x}_{i-1}^{2}-7{y}_{j-1}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f01c6d26-ab1d-5259-bce3-3c519ca1d7d7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f01c6d26-ab1d-5259-bce3-3c519ca1d7d7" :answer-field/id #uuid "f01c6d26-ab1d-5259-bce3-3c519ca1d7d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1c3d1641-cb46-5e92-bf5f-abd201c6c1c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1c3d1641-cb46-5e92-bf5f-abd201c6c1c7" "answer-a29eccc2-e2dd-5f3a-9dff-497bc8cd1a3d" "answer-e7202ccc-39df-5425-8238-49d6ad288b35" "answer-a5559fca-96e9-5818-8eed-c4de766fb047" "answer-de67ebfd-c75a-5de3-a483-c30a7b81d8ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c3d1641-cb46-5e92-bf5f-abd201c6c1c7" :answer/id #uuid "1c3d1641-cb46-5e92-bf5f-abd201c6c1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15-3{x}_{i-1}^{2}-7{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a29eccc2-e2dd-5f3a-9dff-497bc8cd1a3d" :answer/id #uuid "a29eccc2-e2dd-5f3a-9dff-497bc8cd1a3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15-3{x}_{i-1}^{2}-7{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7202ccc-39df-5425-8238-49d6ad288b35" :answer/id #uuid "e7202ccc-39df-5425-8238-49d6ad288b35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15-3{x}_{i}^{2}-7{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5559fca-96e9-5818-8eed-c4de766fb047" :answer/id #uuid "a5559fca-96e9-5818-8eed-c4de766fb047" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de67ebfd-c75a-5de3-a483-c30a7b81d8ca" :answer/id #uuid "de67ebfd-c75a-5de3-a483-c30a7b81d8ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345079 :question/problem "Let $R=[-5,2]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=35-3x-9y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-a1179d1f-26fd-5e6b-8418-2edcb8c92a44" :question/id #uuid "a1179d1f-26fd-5e6b-8418-2edcb8c92a44" :question/math-academy-id "q-123593" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,2]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=y-x+5.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=y-x+5$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=y-x+5$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ff/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/74/74d546d91e145efea49b70af56cb472e8bbbd1417725cd7fa92a3a278cad75ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})={y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}+5)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}+5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ffdf696a-e72a-58a9-802a-4f71c3a5a72c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ffdf696a-e72a-58a9-802a-4f71c3a5a72c" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffdf696a-e72a-58a9-802a-4f71c3a5a72c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2867ca93-342a-5654-9df2-3bbebf7bb504" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1c1d85b-4aff-5b42-9539-203271a62e7b" "answer-9f1a6627-dd31-54c2-b96a-284f2c6ac163" "answer-aab46e2e-7369-5016-9017-bc31144f6951" "answer-2867ca93-342a-5654-9df2-3bbebf7bb504" "answer-a9ed1faf-e588-5474-a09f-6fabf8b6ac66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1c1d85b-4aff-5b42-9539-203271a62e7b" :answer/id #uuid "f1c1d85b-4aff-5b42-9539-203271a62e7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}_{j-1}+{x}_{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f1a6627-dd31-54c2-b96a-284f2c6ac163" :answer/id #uuid "9f1a6627-dd31-54c2-b96a-284f2c6ac163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}_{j}+{x}_{i-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aab46e2e-7369-5016-9017-bc31144f6951" :answer/id #uuid "aab46e2e-7369-5016-9017-bc31144f6951" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i-1}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2867ca93-342a-5654-9df2-3bbebf7bb504" :answer/id #uuid "2867ca93-342a-5654-9df2-3bbebf7bb504" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9ed1faf-e588-5474-a09f-6fabf8b6ac66" :answer/id #uuid "a9ed1faf-e588-5474-a09f-6fabf8b6ac66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{j}-{x}_{i}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ffb8ae0d-deff-51a0-b378-8457bd7de602" :question/id #uuid "ffb8ae0d-deff-51a0-b378-8457bd7de602" :question/math-academy-id "q-122842" :question/problem "Let $R=[-3,2]\\times [-5,-4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=4x-y+9.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$\nwhat is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=4x-y+9$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=4x-y+9$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/de/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=4{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}+9)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}+9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6e000c01-49d3-5298-bef9-8c3d3f78054e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6e000c01-49d3-5298-bef9-8c3d3f78054e" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e000c01-49d3-5298-bef9-8c3d3f78054e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e5afd2f8-e31a-5143-828c-770cbb2a9a27" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d89ba976-b035-52fe-abf9-c063f8d46052" "answer-e4e3ce7f-3fd0-512a-a4fa-ec79e8f97f09" "answer-c3d73011-034b-5713-8b7e-b2d6cb6feedf" "answer-e5afd2f8-e31a-5143-828c-770cbb2a9a27" "answer-90f420f3-4dfa-5dcb-803a-eb38ecfc173a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d89ba976-b035-52fe-abf9-c063f8d46052" :answer/id #uuid "d89ba976-b035-52fe-abf9-c063f8d46052" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4e3ce7f-3fd0-512a-a4fa-ec79e8f97f09" :answer/id #uuid "e4e3ce7f-3fd0-512a-a4fa-ec79e8f97f09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3d73011-034b-5713-8b7e-b2d6cb6feedf" :answer/id #uuid "c3d73011-034b-5713-8b7e-b2d6cb6feedf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5afd2f8-e31a-5143-828c-770cbb2a9a27" :answer/id #uuid "e5afd2f8-e31a-5143-828c-770cbb2a9a27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90f420f3-4dfa-5dcb-803a-eb38ecfc173a" :answer/id #uuid "90f420f3-4dfa-5dcb-803a-eb38ecfc173a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-450ac2a6-bf41-5a0f-9075-7209697c621b" :question/id #uuid "450ac2a6-bf41-5a0f-9075-7209697c621b" :question/math-academy-id "q-123591" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,2]\\times [-1,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5y-3x+20.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5y-3x+20$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5y-3x+20$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ff/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/74/74d546d91e145efea49b70af56cb472e8bbbd1417725cd7fa92a3a278cad75ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=5{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}+20)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}+20.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7c8671f0-4895-504f-af81-8c56f24f54e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7c8671f0-4895-504f-af81-8c56f24f54e9" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c8671f0-4895-504f-af81-8c56f24f54e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4747c65d-9a96-5931-b54a-a40d4a87781c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-58dd5df9-ee4b-5f6d-8004-5d17d0dbceef" "answer-ca03f9fe-7d4d-513f-a4bc-c936ca5157c2" "answer-852ac524-09a0-5c1c-ba70-55984dc179f8" "answer-4747c65d-9a96-5931-b54a-a40d4a87781c" "answer-a5b1273e-b54e-5000-9cc5-2076f306c867"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58dd5df9-ee4b-5f6d-8004-5d17d0dbceef" :answer/id #uuid "58dd5df9-ee4b-5f6d-8004-5d17d0dbceef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}_{j-1}+{x}_{i-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca03f9fe-7d4d-513f-a4bc-c936ca5157c2" :answer/id #uuid "ca03f9fe-7d4d-513f-a4bc-c936ca5157c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}_{j}+{x}_{i-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-852ac524-09a0-5c1c-ba70-55984dc179f8" :answer/id #uuid "852ac524-09a0-5c1c-ba70-55984dc179f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{y}_{j-1}-3{x}_{i-1}+20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4747c65d-9a96-5931-b54a-a40d4a87781c" :answer/id #uuid "4747c65d-9a96-5931-b54a-a40d4a87781c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}+20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5b1273e-b54e-5000-9cc5-2076f306c867" :answer/id #uuid "a5b1273e-b54e-5000-9cc5-2076f306c867" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i}+20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186112872 :answer-field/choices 17592186112873] [:db/retract 17592186112872 :answer-field/choices 17592186112874] [:db/retract 17592186112872 :answer-field/choices 17592186112875] [:db/retract 17592186112872 :answer-field/choices 17592186112876] [:db/retract 17592186112872 :answer-field/choices 17592186112877] {:db/id 17592186489170 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-545ece5b-8e3c-584b-b6c7-99fcc1c7f1e4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-545ece5b-8e3c-584b-b6c7-99fcc1c7f1e4" :question/id #uuid "545ece5b-8e3c-584b-b6c7-99fcc1c7f1e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-223771" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are rational?\n\nI. $0.1222$\n\nII. $1.3\\overset{―}{4}$\n\nIII. $1.981354…$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our numbers in turn.\n\n- $0.1222$ is a rational number because it can be expressed as a ratio of two integers:\n\n$$\n0.1222=\\frac{1\\,222}{10\\,000}\n$$\n\n- $1.3\\overset{―}{4}$ is a rational number. The notation $\\overset{―}{4}$ tells us that the digit $4$ after the decimal point repeats indefinitely.\n\n$$\n1.3\\overset{―}{4}=1.34444444444…\n$$\n\nAny decimal with repeating digits can be represented as a ratio of two integers. In this case,\n\n$$\n1.3\\overset{―}{4}=\\frac{121}{90}.\n$$\n\n- $1.981354…$ is not a rational number. The notation \"$…$\" tells us that digits after the decimal point extend forever. However, there are no repeating digits.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bcc79105-671c-5be0-a88d-c239f34d4061"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bcc79105-671c-5be0-a88d-c239f34d4061" :answer-field/id #uuid "bcc79105-671c-5be0-a88d-c239f34d4061" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-25a5696c-a26b-502d-be4e-0afdfd7f51f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25a5696c-a26b-502d-be4e-0afdfd7f51f8" "answer-e29ca0b9-8013-5e7c-88ee-a18445c629ff" "answer-fd529219-bbce-5ad9-9500-b1576186d994" "answer-1d6bfadd-7df2-5a71-bdb1-030ca706906d" "answer-fe3331e6-1d14-5f24-9a05-99b572f9ab12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25a5696c-a26b-502d-be4e-0afdfd7f51f8" :answer/id #uuid "25a5696c-a26b-502d-be4e-0afdfd7f51f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e29ca0b9-8013-5e7c-88ee-a18445c629ff" :answer/id #uuid "e29ca0b9-8013-5e7c-88ee-a18445c629ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd529219-bbce-5ad9-9500-b1576186d994" :answer/id #uuid "fd529219-bbce-5ad9-9500-b1576186d994" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d6bfadd-7df2-5a71-bdb1-030ca706906d" :answer/id #uuid "1d6bfadd-7df2-5a71-bdb1-030ca706906d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe3331e6-1d14-5f24-9a05-99b572f9ab12" :answer/id #uuid "fe3331e6-1d14-5f24-9a05-99b572f9ab12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115651 :question/problem "![](images/ef/ef8e883c83a32ae5ece92686a73ec1c1210d92074d33d4a2e44572add51a88ee.png)\n\nOn which interval(s) is the function $y=f(x)$, shown above, increasing?" :question/worked-solution "If we follow the graph from left to right, we can see that: \n\n- For $x\\in (-\\infty ,0)$ the graph rises\n\n- For $x\\in (0,1)$ the graph falls\n\n- For $x\\in (1,\\infty )$ the graph rises\n\nThe function is increasing on the intervals where it never falls: $(-\\infty ,0)$ and $(1,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186112872 :answer-field/correct "answer-8cda3b06-fc65-539f-a0fe-5a74cf66c1f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1ad65148-e01b-5814-8603-c310e6c136e8" "answer-8cda3b06-fc65-539f-a0fe-5a74cf66c1f1" "answer-063a7b7f-b47f-5420-8652-88b2a645f008" "answer-548e25f6-f4e6-533b-b1ed-f0e56a335f22" "answer-5fa45410-4390-591e-b4d0-2cfa50c312c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ad65148-e01b-5814-8603-c310e6c136e8" :answer/id #uuid "1ad65148-e01b-5814-8603-c310e6c136e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-\\infty ,0)$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cda3b06-fc65-539f-a0fe-5a74cf66c1f1" :answer/id #uuid "8cda3b06-fc65-539f-a0fe-5a74cf66c1f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-\\infty ,0)$ and $(1,\\infty )$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-063a7b7f-b47f-5420-8652-88b2a645f008" :answer/id #uuid "063a7b7f-b47f-5420-8652-88b2a645f008" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-\\infty ,1)$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-548e25f6-f4e6-533b-b1ed-f0e56a335f22" :answer/id #uuid "548e25f6-f4e6-533b-b1ed-f0e56a335f22" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,\\infty )$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fa45410-4390-591e-b4d0-2cfa50c312c3" :answer/id #uuid "5fa45410-4390-591e-b4d0-2cfa50c312c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,\\infty )$   only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176015 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ef0090d7-e552-5522-8456-ce718437e171"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ef0090d7-e552-5522-8456-ce718437e171" :question/id #uuid "ef0090d7-e552-5522-8456-ce718437e171" :question/math-academy-id "q-120407" :question/problem "The time, in hours, it takes to empty a pool varies inversely with the rate of pumping, in gallons per hour ($\\text{gph}$). If it takes $5$ hours to empty the pool at a rate of $200\\,\\text{gph},$ what is the constant of variation?" :question/worked-solution "The time $t$ is inversely proportional to the rate of pumping $r,$ so we have\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{k}{r},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is the constant of variation.\n\nWe are told that it takes $5$ hours to empty the pool at a rate of $200\\,\\text{gph}.$  We can use this information to solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =\\frac{k}{200} \\\\ 5\\cdot 200 & =k \\\\ 1\\,000 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our final answer is $k=1\\,000.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-deb9d83a-08d5-565b-aa43-4570ecfc8e23"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-deb9d83a-08d5-565b-aa43-4570ecfc8e23" :answer-field/id #uuid "deb9d83a-08d5-565b-aa43-4570ecfc8e23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-72de3c79-c429-510b-a5a0-9e53f9ea6288" :answer-field/choices ["answer-72a5b4a1-8899-5c56-bdf0-2ccfcab5d58d" "answer-c3da19e8-a0a3-53c5-9a36-500ef3112bce" "answer-72de3c79-c429-510b-a5a0-9e53f9ea6288" "answer-8e03c3b2-9b01-57f9-a12b-2c9cdfdf3dd7" "answer-17a716a6-7e4d-54fc-b13f-a601c3ca82e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72a5b4a1-8899-5c56-bdf0-2ccfcab5d58d" :answer/id #uuid "72a5b4a1-8899-5c56-bdf0-2ccfcab5d58d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.025" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3da19e8-a0a3-53c5-9a36-500ef3112bce" :answer/id #uuid "c3da19e8-a0a3-53c5-9a36-500ef3112bce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72de3c79-c429-510b-a5a0-9e53f9ea6288" :answer/id #uuid "72de3c79-c429-510b-a5a0-9e53f9ea6288" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e03c3b2-9b01-57f9-a12b-2c9cdfdf3dd7" :answer/id #uuid "8e03c3b2-9b01-57f9-a12b-2c9cdfdf3dd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17a716a6-7e4d-54fc-b13f-a601c3ca82e5" :answer/id #uuid "17a716a6-7e4d-54fc-b13f-a601c3ca82e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175949 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1a0b67f9-e70a-56fd-9ed9-04486a79a002"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1a0b67f9-e70a-56fd-9ed9-04486a79a002" :question/id #uuid "1a0b67f9-e70a-56fd-9ed9-04486a79a002" :question/math-academy-id "q-80174" :question/problem "Factor $100+40y-5{y}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can factor out a $(-5)$ from each of the terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100+40y-5{y}^{2} & =-5({y}^{2}-8y-20) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the polynomial ${y}^{2}-8y-20$ in parentheses.\n\nWe start by listing the factor pairs of the constant term $(-20).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-20) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 20 \\\\ 2 & \\times (-10) \\\\ (-2) & \\times 10 \\\\ 4 & \\times (-5) \\\\ (-4) & \\times 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-8):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-20) & =-19 & \\times  \\\\ -1+20 & =19 & \\times  \\\\ 2+(-10) & =-8 & ✓ \\\\ -2+10 & =8 & \\times  \\\\ 4+(-5) & =-1 & \\times  \\\\ -4+5 & =1 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, we write the linear term as $-8y=2y-10y$ and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5({y}^{2}-8y-20) & = \\\\ -5({y}^{2}+2y-10y-20) & = \\\\ -5(({y}^{2}+2y)+(-10y-20)) & = \\\\ -5(y(y+2)-10(y+2)) & = \\\\ -5(y-10)(y+2) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-20bcd852-4da7-5c86-b1b8-f77067a480cd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-20bcd852-4da7-5c86-b1b8-f77067a480cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "20bcd852-4da7-5c86-b1b8-f77067a480cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f19b6b7f-625a-51d8-8fa2-fba6b9225227" :answer-field/choices ["answer-70f8bc63-9032-59d6-94c7-44731a339417" "answer-602c6570-8eef-570f-ab39-c5dfd88147f7" "answer-5c8b5761-5505-52d5-b16d-9caf40cd8a5e" "answer-f19b6b7f-625a-51d8-8fa2-fba6b9225227" "answer-8e79ff6b-683b-5305-8568-90663d207d42"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70f8bc63-9032-59d6-94c7-44731a339417" :answer/id #uuid "70f8bc63-9032-59d6-94c7-44731a339417" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-20)(5y+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-602c6570-8eef-570f-ab39-c5dfd88147f7" :answer/id #uuid "602c6570-8eef-570f-ab39-c5dfd88147f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5(y+10)(y-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c8b5761-5505-52d5-b16d-9caf40cd8a5e" :answer/id #uuid "5c8b5761-5505-52d5-b16d-9caf40cd8a5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5(y+5)(y+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f19b6b7f-625a-51d8-8fa2-fba6b9225227" :answer/id #uuid "f19b6b7f-625a-51d8-8fa2-fba6b9225227" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5(y-10)(y+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e79ff6b-683b-5305-8568-90663d207d42" :answer/id #uuid "8e79ff6b-683b-5305-8568-90663d207d42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5(y-5)(y-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068828 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2bd15f40-e989-5300-b551-e3144c2c681f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2bd15f40-e989-5300-b551-e3144c2c681f" :question/id #uuid "2bd15f40-e989-5300-b551-e3144c2c681f" :question/math-academy-id "q-142027" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{288a}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first write $288a$ as the product $144\\cdot 2a$ which contains a perfect square $(144):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{288a} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{144\\cdot 2a} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{144\\cdot 2a} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(12)^{2}\\cdot 2a} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(12)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(12)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} & = \\\\ |12|\\cdot \\sqrt{2a} & = \\\\ 12\\sqrt{2a} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a2b7404d-e71d-5caa-9f77-0a7e4942005f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a2b7404d-e71d-5caa-9f77-0a7e4942005f" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2b7404d-e71d-5caa-9f77-0a7e4942005f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-23f5d581-b735-5062-a71e-32bc76f94353" :answer-field/choices ["answer-23f5d581-b735-5062-a71e-32bc76f94353" "answer-08f452c3-9f2c-5647-b7af-c22e41c80791" "answer-7466ed08-97c1-557f-bae6-81e174a0f8e7" "answer-b7101c8e-c2e8-549e-861f-eeb818e4fc44" "answer-a76e354b-19c7-5276-987d-f27f82fdd8ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23f5d581-b735-5062-a71e-32bc76f94353" :answer/id #uuid "23f5d581-b735-5062-a71e-32bc76f94353" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\sqrt{2a}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08f452c3-9f2c-5647-b7af-c22e41c80791" :answer/id #uuid "08f452c3-9f2c-5647-b7af-c22e41c80791" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12a\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7466ed08-97c1-557f-bae6-81e174a0f8e7" :answer/id #uuid "7466ed08-97c1-557f-bae6-81e174a0f8e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "144\\sqrt{a}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7101c8e-c2e8-549e-861f-eeb818e4fc44" :answer/id #uuid "b7101c8e-c2e8-549e-861f-eeb818e4fc44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\sqrt{a}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a76e354b-19c7-5276-987d-f27f82fdd8ad" :answer/id #uuid "a76e354b-19c7-5276-987d-f27f82fdd8ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{12a}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105751 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f3b5ac18-7c76-53e4-b7d2-3ac62a11ea93"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f3b5ac18-7c76-53e4-b7d2-3ac62a11ea93" :question/id #uuid "f3b5ac18-7c76-53e4-b7d2-3ac62a11ea93" :question/math-academy-id "q-223197" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c543b90535e3b252954ffb9e935f3f05a71d302f1f69a5212b467c826c9d8697.png)\n\nGiven the quadrilateral above, we have $x=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+(6x+{30}^{∘})+(5x+{30}^{∘})+4x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 20x+{60}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 20x & ={300}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68f65a3c-aa44-5a53-857d-09108a8b580f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68f65a3c-aa44-5a53-857d-09108a8b580f" :answer-field/id #uuid "68f65a3c-aa44-5a53-857d-09108a8b580f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c93084f1-f47b-56e6-bf6d-5ad197d70732" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c93084f1-f47b-56e6-bf6d-5ad197d70732"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c93084f1-f47b-56e6-bf6d-5ad197d70732" :answer/id #uuid "c93084f1-f47b-56e6-bf6d-5ad197d70732" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110661 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-11621803-c2eb-5773-8ffe-0f4ac7a22e24"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-11621803-c2eb-5773-8ffe-0f4ac7a22e24" :question/id #uuid "11621803-c2eb-5773-8ffe-0f4ac7a22e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-141985" :question/problem "${x}^{2}y\\cdot {({x}^{3}y)}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We start by using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y\\cdot {({x}^{3}y)}^{2}={x}^{2}y\\cdot ({x}^{3})^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y\\cdot ({x}^{3})^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}y\\cdot {x}^{3\\cdot 2}\\cdot {y}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}y\\cdot {x}^{6}\\cdot {y}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y\\cdot {x}^{6}\\cdot {y}^{2} & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{6})\\cdot (y\\cdot {y}^{2}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2+6}\\cdot {y}^{1+2} & = \\\\ {x}^{8}\\cdot {y}^{3} & = \\\\ {x}^{8}{y}^{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-30f3163e-b6a0-5c37-924e-1f4431be9678"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-30f3163e-b6a0-5c37-924e-1f4431be9678" :answer-field/id #uuid "30f3163e-b6a0-5c37-924e-1f4431be9678" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb228a61-3f9d-5659-ae9c-8dfd49bbaa74" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6eb87bf4-b704-5e70-b4f3-5261c9ecd7a4" "answer-16d4aa1a-69ae-5b4c-a5e7-5285bd50e819" "answer-dfe2668c-035e-5e9f-aaa8-412ae410941d" "answer-d44100e7-af02-52ab-9908-f002db669ae1" "answer-cb228a61-3f9d-5659-ae9c-8dfd49bbaa74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6eb87bf4-b704-5e70-b4f3-5261c9ecd7a4" :answer/id #uuid "6eb87bf4-b704-5e70-b4f3-5261c9ecd7a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{10}{y}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16d4aa1a-69ae-5b4c-a5e7-5285bd50e819" :answer/id #uuid "16d4aa1a-69ae-5b4c-a5e7-5285bd50e819" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{11}{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfe2668c-035e-5e9f-aaa8-412ae410941d" :answer/id #uuid "dfe2668c-035e-5e9f-aaa8-412ae410941d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{5}{y}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d44100e7-af02-52ab-9908-f002db669ae1" :answer/id #uuid "d44100e7-af02-52ab-9908-f002db669ae1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{6}{y}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb228a61-3f9d-5659-ae9c-8dfd49bbaa74" :answer/id #uuid "cb228a61-3f9d-5659-ae9c-8dfd49bbaa74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{8}{y}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115336 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2b6ddb3f-4ad3-5b3b-b8b2-23791ddb8dd3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2b6ddb3f-4ad3-5b3b-b8b2-23791ddb8dd3" :question/id #uuid "2b6ddb3f-4ad3-5b3b-b8b2-23791ddb8dd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-166605" :question/problem "![](images/06/06616bd59152ad40f051177a319b6a54c4e6df2c60ba04bc6056fa3ceea98c03.png)\n\nConsider $△PQR$ shown above. The line segment $\\overset{―}{QH}$ is the altitude corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PR}.$ If $m∠QRP={155}^{∘},$ calculate $m∠RQH.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QRP+m∠HRQ & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {155}^{∘}+m∠HRQ & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HRQ & ={25}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $△QHR$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠RQH+m∠HRQ+m∠QHR & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠RQH+{25}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠RQH+{115}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠RQH & ={65}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-18ef1367-2b1e-5456-9cb2-9b7234a263ce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-18ef1367-2b1e-5456-9cb2-9b7234a263ce" :answer-field/id #uuid "18ef1367-2b1e-5456-9cb2-9b7234a263ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e2d7a032-9fb1-56b1-93d9-c578bcbe7781" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c430c6a4-1994-5032-b37e-9d863f70d745" "answer-8c58649b-4e56-5024-8054-56213d633f42" "answer-4e1d21e0-54d6-5074-8014-fd2d69018758" "answer-6273bcce-aef5-5fd0-bccb-2a0969e9fe22" "answer-e2d7a032-9fb1-56b1-93d9-c578bcbe7781"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c430c6a4-1994-5032-b37e-9d863f70d745" :answer/id #uuid "c430c6a4-1994-5032-b37e-9d863f70d745" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c58649b-4e56-5024-8054-56213d633f42" :answer/id #uuid "8c58649b-4e56-5024-8054-56213d633f42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e1d21e0-54d6-5074-8014-fd2d69018758" :answer/id #uuid "4e1d21e0-54d6-5074-8014-fd2d69018758" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6273bcce-aef5-5fd0-bccb-2a0969e9fe22" :answer/id #uuid "6273bcce-aef5-5fd0-bccb-2a0969e9fe22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2d7a032-9fb1-56b1-93d9-c578bcbe7781" :answer/id #uuid "e2d7a032-9fb1-56b1-93d9-c578bcbe7781" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064175 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-737200e6-c3ef-51a6-b724-78dcb92c8633" "question-03c05eb1-a1b5-5135-a57f-9c96b45d2734"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-737200e6-c3ef-51a6-b724-78dcb92c8633" :question/id #uuid "737200e6-c3ef-51a6-b724-78dcb92c8633" :question/math-academy-id "q-28880" :question/problem "Given the inequalities, $x<3$ and $x>-1$, express their common set of solutions as an interval." :question/worked-solution "We start by sketching the solutions to the two inequalities separately:\n\n![](images/16/166ce99c0ceedf97d38066b544b5dc6ff7ca63296572d952536193a83a410d94.png)\n\n![](images/b5/b5a0212c7df84c064e5b49f878c47f824631bf9585bf20a7a48ce8ddc1b4a646.png)\n\nThe common set of values consists of the values that are in both intervals. So, it can be graphed by finding where the two intervals overlap:\n\n![](images/25/25313fabbd318c3c1fdc5e63b0d20ac44b5a4c951f70232dbefaaa2d82db4045.png)\n\nTherefore, the common set of values is\n$(-1,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c748d70c-8464-5ad6-b8fa-7ac841e67513"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c748d70c-8464-5ad6-b8fa-7ac841e67513" :answer-field/id #uuid "c748d70c-8464-5ad6-b8fa-7ac841e67513" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a9dba03-5fa7-5118-ad22-05a191e7c70e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6a9dba03-5fa7-5118-ad22-05a191e7c70e" "answer-317f62a7-f15c-5b8e-a3a7-6ef60ab56f79" "answer-dc21a884-c07c-5990-ba2f-65cfe89ba621" "answer-9504a3ef-f3df-5103-bbbd-484f5fa182cc" "answer-385b92a8-763a-56eb-879a-8d3a16dd0ef1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a9dba03-5fa7-5118-ad22-05a191e7c70e" :answer/id #uuid "6a9dba03-5fa7-5118-ad22-05a191e7c70e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-317f62a7-f15c-5b8e-a3a7-6ef60ab56f79" :answer/id #uuid "317f62a7-f15c-5b8e-a3a7-6ef60ab56f79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc21a884-c07c-5990-ba2f-65cfe89ba621" :answer/id #uuid "dc21a884-c07c-5990-ba2f-65cfe89ba621" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9504a3ef-f3df-5103-bbbd-484f5fa182cc" :answer/id #uuid "9504a3ef-f3df-5103-bbbd-484f5fa182cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-385b92a8-763a-56eb-879a-8d3a16dd0ef1" :answer/id #uuid "385b92a8-763a-56eb-879a-8d3a16dd0ef1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-1,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179818 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c76e6329-2e41-5111-9e2f-17e316c25286"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c76e6329-2e41-5111-9e2f-17e316c25286" :question/id #uuid "c76e6329-2e41-5111-9e2f-17e316c25286" :question/math-academy-id "q-147068" :question/problem "When a coin was tossed $14$ times, $\\frac{4}{7}$ of the tosses landed heads up. How many times did it come up with tails?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of heads to the total number of tosses is $\\frac{4}{7}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of heads, and the denominator represents the total number of tosses.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $14$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\times 2}{7\\times 2}=\\frac{8}{14}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it came up with heads $8$ times. \nSo, the number of tails is\n\n$$\n14-8=6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-966de87a-ff5f-5fa4-bf5e-d284c88f29c3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-966de87a-ff5f-5fa4-bf5e-d284c88f29c3" :answer-field/id #uuid "966de87a-ff5f-5fa4-bf5e-d284c88f29c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-272d75fc-e799-